==English==
{{pedia}}
===Alternative forms===
* {{l|en|pacquet}} {{qualifier|obsolete}}

===Etymology===
Either from {{etyl|frm|en}} {{m|frm|pacquet}}, or formed independently from {{affix|en|pack|-et}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|UK}} {{IPA|/ˈpakɪt/|lang=en}} 
* {{a|US}} {{IPA|/ˈpæ.kɪt/|lang=en}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# A small [[pack]] or [[package]]; a little [[bundle]] or [[parcel]]
#: ''Don't throw the crisp '''packet''' on the floor!''
#: ''a '''packet''' of letters''
#: ''a '''packet''' of crisps''
#: ''a '''packet''' of biscuits''
# {{lb|en|nautical}} Originally, a vessel employed by government to convey dispatches or mails; hence, a vessel employed in conveying dispatches, mails, passengers, and goods, and having fixed days of sailing; a mail boat. Packet boat, ship, vessel ([[w:Packet (sea transport)|Wikipedia]]).
#* {{RQ:EHough PrqsPrc|I|0025}}
#*: With just the turn of a shoulder she indicated the water front, where, at the end of the dock on which they stood, lay the good ship, ''Mount Vernon'', river '''packet''', the black smoke already pouring from her stacks.
# {{lb|en|botany}} A [[specimen]] [[envelope]] containing small, dried [[plant]]s or containing parts of plants when attached to a larger sheet.
#* {{RQ:Schuster Hepaticae V|vii}}
#*: With fresh material, taxonomic conclusions are leavened by recognition that the material examined reflects the site it occupied; a herbarium '''packet''' gives one only a small fraction of the data desirable for sound conclusions. Herbarium material does not, indeed, allow one to extrapolate safely: what you see is what you get{{nb...}}.
# {{lb|en|networking}} A small fragment of data as transmitted on some types of [[network]], notably [[Ethernet]] networks ([[w:Network packet|Wikipedia]]).
# {{lb|en|South Africa}} A [[plastic bag]].
#* '''2012''' August 6, [http://www.iol.co.za/blogs/wendy-knowler-s-consumer-watch-1.1608/plastic-packets-who-bags-the-profits-1.1356896#.VIapdsnCfIU Wendy Knowler], ''[http://www.iol.co.za/blogs/wendy-knowler-s-consumer-watch-1.1608/plastic-packets-who-bags-the-profits-1.1356896 Plastic '''packets''': who bags the profits?]

